<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vasily Kosoy</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1448</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Vasily Yuryevich</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vasily Kosoy was a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yury-of-zvenigorod">Yury of Zvenigorod</a> and a contender in the Muscovite civil war of 1425–1453. After his father's death in 1434 he briefly claimed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a>, but he was defeated by his cousin Vasily II, captured in 1436 and blinded, from which he gained his nickname, 'the Squint-eyed'. He died in captivity in 1448, while his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dmitry-shemyaka">Dmitry Shemyaka</a> continued the struggle.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vasily-kosoy.jpg" alt="Vasily Kosoy" width="320" height="661" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Мастера Оружейной Палаты: Г. Никитин, С. Савин, Симон Ушаков, С. Резанец, Ф. Зубов, Я. Казанец, И. Владимиров, Ф. Коз... · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Frescos_in_Cathedral_of_the_Archangel_in_Moscow_-_west_wall_01_-_Vasily_Kosoy.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
